      "math_academy_id": "q-73605",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $B?$\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
